From: =?UTF-8?q?Jean-Micha=C3=ABl=20Celerier?=
 <jeanmichael.celerier@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 16:56:19 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] rhi: gl: no min filter on multisample textures

QGles2Texture::create() set GL_TEXTURE_MIN_FILTER unconditionally,
including on GL_TEXTURE_2D_MULTISAMPLE textures, which take no sampler
state: every multisample texture (e.g. Qt Quick 3D's MSAA render
texture) raised GL_INVALID_ENUM. Skip it when samples > 1.
---
 src/gui/rhi/qrhigles2.cpp | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/gui/rhi/qrhigles2.cpp b/src/gui/rhi/qrhigles2.cpp
index 96d45c4d7..861cb3fee 100644
--- a/src/gui/rhi/qrhigles2.cpp
+++ b/src/gui/rhi/qrhigles2.cpp
@@ -6754,7 +6754,9 @@ bool QGles2Texture::create()
         // here, given the ridiculous default of GL. It is changed based on
         // the sampler later, but there could be cases when one pulls the native
         // object out via nativeTexture() right away.
-        rhiD->f->glTexParameteri(target, GL_TEXTURE_MIN_FILTER, GL_LINEAR);
+        // Multisample textures take no sampler state: GL_INVALID_ENUM.
+        if (samples <= 1)
+            rhiD->f->glTexParameteri(target, GL_TEXTURE_MIN_FILTER, GL_LINEAR);
         specified = true;
     } else {
         // Cannot use glCompressedTexImage2D without valid data, so defer.
-- 
